      "text": "To find the volume of a frustum, we need to first determine the volume of the original pyramid and the volume of the smaller pyramid formed above the cut.\nThe volume of a pyramid is given by $\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{base area} \\times \\text{height}$. So, the volume of the original pyramid is $\\frac{1}{3} \\times 12^2 \\times 8 = 384$ cubic centimeters.\nThe volume of the smaller pyramid is $\\frac{1}{3} \\times 6^2 \\times 4 = 48$ cubic centimeters.\nSince the larger and smaller pyramids are similar, their corresponding sides are also proportional. In this case, the ratio of their base edges is $12/6 = 2$. This means that the 4 cm altitude of the smaller pyramid is $8 cm \\div 2 = 4 cm$. \nTherefore, the volume of the frustum is the volume of the original pyramid minus the volume of the smaller pyramid, or $\\boxed{336}$ cubic centimeters.",
