      "text": "Step 1: Find the volume of the wooden model of the pyramid.\nThe volume of a pyramid is given by the formula V = (1/3) * B * h, where B is the area of the base and h is the altitude.\nFor the larger pyramid, the base edge is 12 cm, so the area of the base is 12 * 12 = 144 square centimeters.\nFor the smaller pyramid, the base edge is 6 cm, so the area of the base is 6 * 6 = 36 square centimeters.\nThe altitude of the larger pyramid is 8 cm, and the altitude of the smaller pyramid is 4 cm, which is half of the altitude of the larger pyramid. This means that the smaller pyramid is similar to the larger pyramid, and the volume of the smaller pyramid is one-fourth of the volume of the larger pyramid.\n\nStep 2: Find the volume of the smaller pyramid.\nSince the smaller pyramid is half the size of the larger pyramid, we divide the volume of the larger pyramid by 4 to find the volume of the smaller pyramid.\nThe volume of the larger pyramid is (1/3) * 144 * 8 = 384 cubic centimeters.\nSo the volume of the smaller pyramid is (1/4) * 384 = 96 cubic centimeters.\n\nStep 3: Find the volume of the frustum.\nThe volume of the frustum is the volume of the larger pyramid minus the volume of the smaller pyramid.\nThe volume of the frustum is 384 - 96 = 288 cubic centimeters.\n\nThe answer is \\boxed{288}.",
