      "text": "To find the volume of the frustum, we first need to calculate the volume of the entire square-based pyramid and then subtract the volume of the smaller pyramid and the area of the usable top part of the original pyramid.\n\nVolume of the original pyramid:\n\\[V_{5} = \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot a_{5} \\cdot h_{5} = \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 12 \\cdot 8 = 32 \\, {\\rm cm}^3\\]\n\nNow, let's calculate the volume of the smaller pyramid with base edges 6*6*6 cm and 4.8*4.8*4.8 cm:\n\nVolume of the smaller pyramid:\n\\[V_{4} = \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot a_{4} \\cdot h_{4} = \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 6 \\cdot 4 \\approx 24 \\, {\\rm cm}^3\\]\n\nThe total volume of both the smaller pyramid and the top part of its original pyramid is:\n\n\\[V_{\\text{top/top}} = V_{4} + (a_{5} h_{5}) = 24 + (12 \\times 8) = 168 \\, {\\rm cm}^3\\]\n\nFinally, the volume of the frustum is the volume of the original pyramid minus the sum of the smaller pyramid's volume and the top part of the original pyramid:\n\n\\[V_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{5} - V_{\\text{top}} = 32 - 168 = -136 \\, {\\rm cm}^3\\]\n\nThe negative result means that these parts are not reasonable in this context. Recalculate the volume of the frustum by removing the volume of the top and bottom parts from the remaining pyramid volume for the original pyramid:\n\n\\[V_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{5} - V_{\\text{top}} - V_{\\text{bottom}}\\]\n\nSince the top part is removed, subtract its volume:\n\n\\[V_{\\text{frustum}} = 32 - V_{\\text{top}} = 32 - (12 \\cdot 8) = 16 \\, {\\rm cm}^3\\]\n\nThere was an error in the second part of the calculation where the smaller pyramid's volume was doubled. So, the final calculation is:\n\n\\[V_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{5} - (V_{\\text{top}} + V_{\\text{angle}})\\]\n\n\\[V_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{5} - (V_{\\text{top}} + V_{4})\\]\n\n\\[V_{\\text{frustum}} = 32 - (12 \\cdot 8) - (a_{4} \\cdot h_{4})\\]\n\n\\[V_{\\text{frustum}} = 32 - 96 - 96 = -148\\]\n\nSince calculations within the pyramid volume subtraction are aspirated as they're negative, we must abandon the result: \n\n\\(\\boxed{-148}\\) cubic centimeters.",
